@startuml 10-seat-state
skinparam backgroundColor White
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Sans
skinparam roundCorner 6
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFFF0
skinparam NoteBorderColor #999999
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F4F4F8
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #555555
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor #F4F4F8
skinparam ClassBorderColor #555555
skinparam StateBackgroundColor #F4F4F8
skinparam StateBorderColor #555555
skinparam ComponentBackgroundColor #F4F4F8
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #555555
title Lifecycle of a single seat within one showtime

[*] --> Free : showtime created\n(SeatMap constructed, all seats Free)

state Free #E8FFE8
state Booked #FFE8E8

Free --> Booked : Catalog::bookSeats()\n**inside the critical section**
Booked --> Free : Catalog::cancelBooking()\nDELETE /api/v1/bookings/{id}

Free --> Free : a concurrent request for a\n*different* seat - no effect
Booked --> Booked : another bookSeats() for this seat\nthrows **SeatUnavailable** (409);\nthe state does not change

Booked --> [*] : showtime removed,\nor its movie/theater removed
Free --> [*] : showtime removed

note right of Free
  Listed in `available_seats`.
  A client being *shown* a free seat is
  not a reservation - the state can change
  before the booking request arrives.
end note

note right of Booked
  Listed in `booked_seats`.
  This is a terminal state for the booking
  that holds it, until that booking is
  cancelled.
end note

note as N1 #FFF8E0
  **Layout changes (PUT /admin/theaters/{id})**

  A relayout preserves seats *by label*:
  a seat booked as "b1" stays "b1" as long as
  "b1" still exists in the new layout.

  * growing  - always safe
  * shrinking - **refused with 409** if any seat
    that would disappear is Booked. Silently
    dropping a paid-for seat is exactly the
    failure this service exists to prevent.

  The new layout is built to one side first, so a
  refusal leaves the original completely untouched
  (the strong exception guarantee).
end note

@enduml
